CSO (Concurrent Servicing Operation) is the simultaneous fueling and/or refueling of an aircraft with other operations such as munitions loading/unloading, aircraft reconfiguration, aircraft –6 Technical Order inspections, and additional servicing like oil, nitrogen, and hydraulic fluid. The activities that are performed when a Chief Servicing Supervisor (CSS) is present include:

• Simultaneous fuel servicing with aircraft –6 and –6WC inspections;
• Simultaneous fuel servicing with munitions/ammunition loading or unloading;
• Simultaneous fuel servicing with aircraft reconfiguration;
• Simultaneous fuel servicing with other aircraft servicing such as oil, nitrogen, and hydraulic fluid;
• Simultaneous fuel servicing that combines any of the above (loading/unloading of munitions, reconfiguration, –6 TO inspections, and other servicing).  In addition, the CSS is the on‑site supervisor responsible for controlling and monitoring all concurrent servicing operations and ensuring safety and compliance.
